:cb_alice_control a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Max's Control Is Love"@en ; :beliefContent "Max's control of my sexuality is his love and commitment to me." ; :beliefStrength "0.75" ; :beliefOrigin "Max's explanations, experience" ; :description "Belief that Max's control is expression of love, not domination. Control shows investment in relationship. This reframes control as care. Belief helps accept denial as gift, not loss."@en ; :leadsTo :to_alice_high .

:cb_alice_purity a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Purity Is Virtue"@en ; :beliefContent "Sexual purity and restraint are virtues. Denial makes me better." ; :beliefStrength "0.8" ; :beliefOrigin "Traditional values, Max's framing" ; :description "Core belief that purity (chastity) is virtuous. Denial is not punishment but moral improvement. This belief helps endure frustration. Purity makes her worthy of Max. Belief is strengthening through training."@en ; :leadsTo :cs_alice_denial_virtue .

:cb_alice_wifely_duty a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Wifely Duty Is Submission"@en ; :beliefContent "A good wife submits to her husband's wishes, including sexual control." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Traditional values, Max's expectations" ; :description "Belief that wifely duty includes sexual submission. Chastity is Max's right as husband-to-be. This belief justifies denial as duty, not deprivation. Duty feels honorable, not oppressive."@en ; :leadsTo :po_alice_submissive .

:cb_anne_punishment a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "I Deserve Punishment"@en ; :beliefContent "My betrayal deserves punishment. Punishment is just and purifying." ; :beliefStrength "0.75" ; :beliefOrigin "Guilt, Leo's punishment, relief from punishment" ; :description "Belief that she deserves punishment for betrayal. Punishment from Leo is just and even relieving. Punishment purifies guilt temporarily. This belief makes her receptive to Leo's discipline. Punishment is both penalty and therapy."@en .

:cb_anne_redemption a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "I Must Earn Redemption"@en ; :beliefContent "I betrayed Leo. I must earn redemption through service and suffering." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Affair guilt, divorce consequences" ; :description "Core belief that redemption must be earned. Betrayal of Leo created debt that must be paid. Service to Leo (training Becky, maintaining household) is payment. Suffering (punishment from Leo) is purification. Redemption may not be possible but must be pursued."@en ; :leadsTo :cb_anne_service, :cb_anne_punishment .

:cb_anne_service a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Service Is My Obligation"@en ; :beliefContent "Serving Leo is my obligation and path to redemption." ; :beliefStrength "0.8" ; :beliefOrigin "Guilt, Leo's expectations" ; :description "Belief that service to Leo is obligation. Training Becky, maintaining household, submitting to Leo - all are service. Service is not choice but duty. Through service, redemption is possible. This belief motivates compliance and excellence."@en .

:cb_becky_belonging a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "I Need to Belong to Someone"@en ; :beliefContent "I am meant to belong to someone. Being owned is my natural state." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Natural submissive orientation, Leo's framing" ; :description "Core belief that she is meant to be owned. This feels like discovering true nature rather than adopting new identity. Belonging to Leo/Anne provides clarity and purpose. This belief conflicts with conventional expectations of independence."@en ; :leadsTo :ds_becky_surrender .

:cb_becky_pain a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Pain Connects Me to My Owners"@en ; :beliefContent "Pain from my owners is a form of love and connection." ; :beliefStrength "0.75" ; :beliefOrigin "Training sessions, aftercare experiences" ; :description "Belief that pain is connection, not punishment (or punishment that leads to connection). Pain from Leo/Anne feels like being claimed. This reframing allows her to accept and even seek pain. Pain becomes pathway to belonging."@en .

:cb_becky_service a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Service Is My Purpose"@en ; :beliefContent "Serving others, especially my owners, is my highest purpose." ; :beliefStrength "0.8" ; :beliefOrigin "Training experiences, natural inclination" ; :description "Belief that service is her purpose. Serving Leo/Anne feels meaningful in way that college tasks don't. Service provides clear metrics for success (pleasing owners) vs. ambiguous college success. This belief is strengthening through training."@en .

:cb_beth_duty a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Duty Above All"@en ; :beliefContent "My duty is to do my job well, no complaints." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Work ethic, survival" ; :description "Belief in duty above personal comfort. Job must be done regardless of difficulty. This enables enduring demanding conditions. Duty is moral framework."@en .

:cb_beth_invisibility a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Invisibility Is Safety"@en ; :beliefContent "Being unnoticed keeps me safe. Don't draw attention." ; :beliefStrength "0.8" ; :beliefOrigin "Class dynamics, self-protection" ; :description "Belief that invisibility provides safety. Not being noticed means not being targeted. This drives quiet, efficient service. Invisibility is protective strategy."@en ; :leadsTo :sc_beth_invisible, :fs_beth_job_loss .

:cb_beth_service a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Service Is My Role"@en ; :beliefContent "I am meant to serve. Service is my purpose and livelihood." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Economic necessity, life experience" ; :description "Core belief that service is her role in life. Not kink but livelihood. Serving Anne is job and identity. This belief enables acceptance of demanding conditions."@en ; :leadsTo :vs_beth_work_ethic .

:cb_bree_control a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "I Must Maintain Control to Be Safe"@en ; :beliefContent "Loss of control leads to danger. I must stay in control of my emotions, body, and situation." ; :beliefStrength "0.8" ; :beliefOrigin "Religious messaging about sin, adolescent shame experiences" ; :description "Belief that control equals safety and loss of control equals danger. Applies to emotions (don't feel too much), body (don't be sexual), and situations (plan everything). BDSM exploration threatens this core belief by requiring surrender of control."@en ; :protectsAgainst :fs_bree_loss ; :challenges :eb_bree_repressed .

:cb_bree_goodness a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "I Must Be Good to Be Loved"@en ; :beliefContent "My worth depends on being good, obedient, and meeting others' expectations. Bad girls are unlovable." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Religious upbringing, parental conditional love" ; :description "Core belief that love and acceptance are contingent on being good. Goodness defined as obedience, purity, traditional behavior. Badness = curiosity about forbidden topics, sexual desire, questioning authority. This belief drives people-pleasing and shame when desires emerge."@en ; :protectsAgainst :rw_bree_judgment ; :undermines :ds_bree_truth .

:cb_bree_shame a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "My Desires Are Wrong"@en ; :beliefContent "Natural curiosity and sexual desire are sinful/dangerous. I should not want what I want." ; :beliefStrength "0.75" ; :beliefOrigin "Religious sexual shame, peer reinforcement (Melissa, Teagan)" ; :description "Deep belief that natural desires, especially sexual curiosity, are wrong. Desires should be suppressed or eliminated. This creates internal war between authentic curiosity and shame about having curiosity."@en ; :leadsTo :sh_bree_desire ; :suppresses :ds_bree_truth .

:cb_edward_inadequacy a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "I Am Inadequate"@en ; :beliefContent "I am not good enough. I fail at everything." ; :beliefStrength "0.8" ; :beliefOrigin "Social rejection, employment failures" ; :description "Core belief of inadequacy. Sees self as failure. This drives resentment and defensiveness. Belief is self-fulfilling - expects failure, creates failure."@en ; :leadsTo :sh_edward_inadequacy .

:cb_edward_punishment a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "The World Owes Me"@en ; :beliefContent "The world has wronged me. I am owed compensation." ; :beliefStrength "0.6" ; :beliefOrigin "Perceived injustices, failures" ; :description "Belief that world owes him. Failures are others' fault. This protects from self-blame but creates entitlement. Entitlement fuels resentment."@en .

:cb_edward_service a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Service Is Below Me"@en ; :beliefContent "I deserve better than this servitude. This is beneath me." ; :beliefStrength "0.7" ; :beliefOrigin "Resentment, unfulfilled expectations" ; :description "Belief that service is beneath him. Resents position, feels deserving of better. This creates conflict - needs job but hates it. Resentment fuels volatility."@en .

:cb_leo_control a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Control Is Everything"@en ; :beliefContent "Control is the only safety. Chaos is the only sin." ; :beliefStrength "0.95" ; :beliefOrigin "Divorce trauma, natural temperament" ; :description "Core belief that control equals safety. Chaos (emotional, situational) is intolerable. This drives dominance - controlling scenes, partners, outcomes. Control is not just preference but existential need. Becky's training is exercise in control."@en ; :leadsTo :fs_leo_chaos, :co_leo_holding .

:cb_leo_discipline a :CoreBelief ; rdfs:label "Discipline Creates Excellence"@en ; :beliefContent "Through discipline and punishment, excellence emerges." ; :beliefStrength "0.85" ; :beliefOrigin "Personal experience, training results" ; :description "Belief that discipline (including physical punishment) creates excellence. Becky's improvement through training confirms this. Punishment is not cruelty but tool for improvement. This belief justifies sadistic practices as benevolent."@en .

