:fd_beth_working_class a :FamilyDynamic ; rdfs:label "Working Class Background"@en ; :familyStructure "Working class family, economic struggles" ; :familyRole "Provider, worker, practical" ; :familyAtmosphere "Survival-focused, pragmatic" ; :parentalStyle "Practical, expecting contribution" ; :description "Working class background with economic struggles. Service work is normal, expected. Family understands employment necessity. BDSM aspects would be concerning but economic need takes precedence."@en .

:fd_bree_conservative a :FamilyDynamic ; rdfs:label "Conservative Religious Family"@en ; :familyStructure "Nuclear family, father as head, mother as homemaker" ; :familyRole "Obedient daughter, good girl, high achiever" ; :familyAtmosphere "Controlled, rule-bound, emotionally restrained, judgmental of outside world" ; :parentalStyle "Authoritarian, conditional love, punishment-based discipline" ; :description "Family operated on clear hierarchy with father at top. Rules were absolute and questioning was rebellion. Emotions were controlled and negative feelings suppressed. Outside world viewed with suspicion. Bree's role was to be the good daughter who made family look respectable through achievement and compliance."@en .

:fd_edward_isolated a :FamilyDynamic ; rdfs:label "Isolated Background"@en ; :familyStructure "Isolated, limited family contact" ; :familyRole "Outsider, disconnected" ; :familyAtmosphere "Distant, unsupportive" ; :parentalStyle "Neglectful or absent" ; :description "Isolated family background. Limited support, connection. This created social difficulties and resentment. Isolation continues - no support network."@en .

