:fe_bree_curiosity a :FormativeExperience ; rdfs:label "Natural Curiosity vs. Religious Prohibition"@en ; :experienceType "Internal conflict" ; :experienceAge "12-18" ; :experienceImpact "0.8" ; :experienceMemory "Secretly reading forbidden books, feeling guilty about curiosity, hiding questions from parents, developing double life"@en ; :description "Adolescent curiosity about world, sexuality, and forbidden topics clashed with religious prohibitions. Developed pattern of secret exploration followed by shame and confession. Learned to compartmentalize curiosity (private) from goodness (public). This split continues in adult life."@en ; :leadsTo :dm_bree_intellectualization, :cs_bree_danger .

:fe_bree_parents a :FormativeExperience ; rdfs:label "Parental Relationship Dynamics"@en ; :experienceType "Family dynamics" ; :experienceAge "0-18" ; :experienceImpact "0.85" ; :experienceMemory "Father as authority figure, mother as enforcer of rules, love conditional on obedience, punishment for questioning"@en ; :description "Father was distant authority figure whose approval was earned through achievement and obedience. Mother enforced rules and monitored behavior for signs of rebellion. Love felt conditional on being good. Questioning authority resulted in withdrawal of affection. Created anxious attachment and approval-seeking."@en ; :leadsTo :ap_bree_anxious, :rn_bree_validation, :rt_bree_authority .

:fe_bree_religious a :FormativeExperience ; rdfs:label "Religious Upbringing"@en ; :experienceType "Religious/conservative household" ; :experienceAge "0-18" ; :experienceImpact "0.9" ; :experienceMemory "Clear memories of church attendance, religious education, sexual shame messaging, good girl expectations"@en ; :description "Raised in conservative Christian household where sex outside marriage was sinful, submission to authority was virtuous, and questioning was discouraged. Sexual curiosity treated as dangerous. Good girl = pure, obedient, traditional. This created deep shame around natural curiosity and desire."@en ; :leadsTo :cb_bree_goodness, :cb_bree_shame, :sh_bree_desire .

