:fn_voyeurism a :Fantasy ; rdfs:label "Voyeurism Fantasy"@en ; :fantasyType "Watching others, observing sex, director role"@en ; :fantasyIntensity "0.65" .

:fs_alice_failure a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Failure"@en ; :fearType "Failure/disappointment" ; :fearIntensity "0.6" ; :fearManagement "0.7" ; :description "Fear organized around failing Max, failing at chastity, disappointing. This fear motivates compliance. Managed through effort and Max's reassurance. Fear is moderate, not debilitating."@en .

:fs_anne_rejection a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Rejection"@en ; :fearType "Rejection/abandonment" ; :fearIntensity "0.8" ; :fearManagement "0.5" ; :description "Fear organized around rejection by Leo. Fears being cast aside, deemed unworthy. This fear drives compliance and service. Management is moderate - functional but anxious. Fear is realistic given history."@en .

:fs_becky_abandonment a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Abandonment"@en ; :fearType "Abandonment/rejection" ; :fearIntensity "0.7" ; :fearManagement "0.6" ; :description "Fear organized around abandonment by Leo/Anne. This fear motivates compliance and service. Managed through consistent reassurance, clear expectations, aftercare. Fear decreases as trust increases."@en .

:fs_beth_job_loss a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Job Loss"@en ; :fearType "Economic/survival" ; :fearIntensity "0.85" ; :fearManagement "0.5" ; :description "Fear organized around job loss. Unemployment is existential threat. This drives compliance. Management is through performance, not resolution."@en .

:fs_bree_loss a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Loss of Control/Safety"@en ; :fearType "Loss of control, loss of safety" ; :fearIntensity "0.75" ; :fearManagement "0.4" ; :description "Fear structure organized around loss of control leading to loss of safety. Control = good/safe. Surrender = bad/dangerous. This makes BDSM exploration particularly threatening. Fear is managed through suppression and intellectualization rather than direct processing."@en .

:fs_edward_abandonment a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Abandonment"@en ; :fearType "Abandonment/rejection" ; :fearIntensity "0.8" ; :fearManagement "0.3" ; :description "Fear organized around abandonment. Fears being cast aside, alone. Management is poor - anxiety is high. Fear drives clinging and resentment."@en .

:fs_leo_chaos a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Chaos"@en ; :fearType "Chaos/loss of control" ; :fearIntensity "0.9" ; :fearManagement "0.7" ; :description "Core fear is chaos - emotional, situational, relational. Loss of control is existential threat. This fear drives dominance and control behaviors. Managed through rigid structure, rules, protocols. Chaos is enemy to be defeated."@en .

:fs_max_infidelity a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Infidelity"@en ; :fearType "Infidelity/betrayal" ; :fearIntensity "0.6" ; :fearManagement "0.8" ; :description "Fear organized around Alice's potential infidelity. Chastity manages this fear. Fear is moderate, not obsessive. Management is through control."@en .

:fs_nolan_harm a :FearStructure ; rdfs:label "Fear Structure - Harm to Community"@en ; :fearType "Community harm, member safety" ; :fearIntensity "0.7" ; :fearManagement "0.8" ; :description "Fear organized around harm to community members. Not personal harm but harm to those in his care. This fear is managed through thorough screening, clear rules, active monitoring. Fear is functional - motivates protection without paralyzing."@en .

:ge_alice_acceptance a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Accepting Long-Term Denial"@en ; :edgeType "Sexual/emotional" ; :edgeChallenge "Accepting permanent or long-term sexual denial" ; :edgeGrowth "Peaceful acceptance of chastity as lifestyle" ; :description "Growth edge is accepting long-term denial. Currently manages frustration, but full acceptance means peace with chastity. This means finding fulfillment outside sexual release. Acceptance would reduce internal conflict."@en .

:ge_alice_frustration_tolerance a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Increasing Frustration Tolerance"@en ; :edgeType "Emotional regulation" ; :edgeChallenge "Building capacity to endure sexual frustration" ; :edgeGrowth "High tolerance for denial without distress" ; :description "Growth edge around frustration tolerance. Currently manages but still struggles. Growth means increased capacity without distress. This comes through time, practice, reframing. Tolerance would improve quality of life."@en .

:ge_anne_honesty a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Radical Honesty"@en ; :edgeType "Relational/ethical" ; :edgeChallenge "Being fully honest with Leo and herself" ; :edgeGrowth "Authentic, honest relationships" ; :description "Growth edge around honesty. Affair was deception. Growth means radical honesty with Leo (about feelings, struggles) and herself (about motives, desires). Honesty is path to authentic redemption. This is frightening but necessary."@en .

:ge_anne_integration a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Integrating Mistress and Penitent"@en ; :edgeType "Identity integration" ; :edgeChallenge "Integrating dominant mistress and penitent servant selves" ; :edgeGrowth "Coherent identity honoring both aspects" ; :description "Growth edge is integrating split identity. Mistress and penitent must become one self. Integration means accepting both guilt and power, both service and dominance. This is core developmental task. Integration would reduce internal tension."@en .

:ge_becky_acceptance a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Accepting Slave Identity"@en ; :edgeType "Identity integration" ; :edgeChallenge "Fully accepting slave identity despite social expectations" ; :edgeGrowth "Integrated identity as owned slave" ; :description "Growth edge is fully accepting slave identity. This means letting go of conventional expectations (career, independence) and embracing ownership. Negotiation with Leo/Anne was step toward acceptance. Full acceptance will bring peace and clarity."@en .

:ge_becky_integration a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Integrating Student and Slave"@en ; :edgeType "Life integration" ; :edgeChallenge "Integrating college life with slave life" ; :edgeGrowth "Coherent life structure honoring both roles" ; :description "Growth edge around integrating college and slave roles. May need to modify college plans to accommodate slave duties. Or find way to make college serve slave role (education that makes better slave). Integration reduces internal conflict."@en .

:ge_beth_self_worth a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Self-Worth Beyond Service"@en ; :edgeType "Identity/value" ; :edgeChallenge "Finding worth beyond service role" ; :edgeGrowth "Intrinsic self-value" ; :description "Growth edge around self-worth. Currently valued for service only. Growth means finding intrinsic worth. This would reduce class shame and improve mental health."@en .

:ge_beth_visibility a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Appropriate Visibility"@en ; :edgeType "Identity/agency" ; :edgeChallenge "Being appropriately visible, asserting needs" ; :edgeGrowth "Balanced visibility and self-advocacy" ; :description "Growth edge around appropriate visibility. Currently invisible. Growth means being seen when appropriate, asserting needs. This would improve wellbeing without threatening security."@en .

:ge_bree_authenticity a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Authentic Self vs. Good Girl"@en ; :edgeType "Identity integration" ; :edgeChallenge "Choosing authenticity over approval" ; :edgeGrowth "Living from authentic values rather than external expectations" ; :description "Growth edge around authenticity vs. people-pleasing. Must choose between being 'good' (Melissa/Teagan's approval) vs. being real (exploring curiosity even when uncomfortable). This is core developmental task of approaching 30 - becoming authentic adult vs. remaining compliant child."@en .

:ge_bree_sexuality a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Sexual Authenticity"@en ; :edgeType "Sexual/erotic development" ; :edgeChallenge "Facing shame about natural curiosity and desire" ; :edgeGrowth "Developing integrated, shame-free sexuality" ; :description "Primary growth edge is developing authentic relationship with sexuality and desire. Requires facing religious shame, questioning internalized messages, allowing curiosity without judgment. Nolan and The Black Collar provide safe container for this exploration. Growth involves moving from repression to integration."@en .

:ge_edward_anger_management a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Anger Management"@en ; :edgeType "Emotional regulation" ; :edgeChallenge "Managing anger without explosion or suppression" ; :edgeGrowth "Healthy anger expression and regulation" ; :description "Critical growth edge is anger management. Current pattern is destructive. Growth means appropriate expression, not suppression or explosion. This is essential for safety."@en .

:ge_edward_self_acceptance a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Self-Acceptance"@en ; :edgeType "Identity/self-worth" ; :edgeChallenge "Accepting self without grandiosity or shame" ; :edgeGrowth "Realistic self-acceptance" ; :description "Growth edge around self-acceptance. Currently oscillates between grandiosity and shame. Growth means realistic self-view. This would reduce volatility."@en .

:ge_leo_sharing a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Sharing Ownership"@en ; :edgeType "Relational/power" ; :edgeChallenge "Sharing Becky's ownership with Anne" ; :edgeGrowth "Collaborative ownership model" ; :description "Growth edge around sharing ownership. Control tendency wants exclusive ownership. Sharing with Anne (7 weeks/2 weekends) requires compromise. This is practice in trust and collaboration. Success would expand capacity for partnership."@en .

:ge_leo_trust a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Learning to Trust Again"@en ; :edgeType "Relational/trust" ; :edgeChallenge "Trusting Anne (and Becky) after betrayal" ; :edgeGrowth "Capacity for vulnerable trust" ; :description "Growth edge is trust. Divorce destroyed trust capacity. Relationship with Anne as submissive tests trust. Shared ownership of Becky requires trusting Anne. Growth means allowing vulnerability despite risk. This is hardest edge."@en .

:ge_max_communication a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Improving Communication About Denial"@en ; :edgeType "Relational/communication" ; :edgeChallenge "Communicating openly with Alice about denial impact" ; :edgeGrowth "Transparent, empathetic communication" ; :description "Growth edge is communication. Can be reticent about Alice's frustration. Growth means discussing denial openly, validating her experience. This would deepen intimacy."@en .

:ge_max_release_flexibility a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Flexibility About Releases"@en ; :edgeType "Behavioral/flexibility" ; :edgeChallenge "Being more flexible about occasional releases" ; :edgeGrowth "Balanced approach to denial and release" ; :description "Growth edge around release flexibility. Tendency is toward strict denial. Growth means occasional releases for Alice's wellbeing. Balance would improve relationship."@en .

:ge_nolan_partnership a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Equal Partnership"@en ; :edgeType "Relational development" ; :edgeChallenge "Finding partner who is equal, not student" ; :edgeGrowth "Mutual relationship with shared power" ; :description "Growth edge around finding equal partnership. Guide/student dynamic is comfortable but limiting. Needs partner who can challenge him, not just learn from him. Bree represents potential - she's outsider but strong, curious, professional. Risk is mixing education with romance."@en .

:ge_nolan_vulnerability a :GrowthEdge ; rdfs:label "Allowing Vulnerability"@en ; :edgeType "Emotional intimacy" ; :edgeChallenge "Allowing himself to be vulnerable, not always the strong one" ; :edgeGrowth "Authentic partnership with mutual vulnerability" ; :description "Growth edge is allowing himself vulnerability. Always the strong one, the protector, the guide. Rarely allows himself to need. With Bree, may find himself wanting to share burden, be seen. This is risky - vulnerability could undermine authority. Growth involves finding partner who can hold his vulnerability."@en .

