:id_alice_chaste a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Chaste Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Chaste/denied" ; :identityCohesion "0.7" ; :identityDiffusion "0.3" ; :description "Identity is organized around chastity. Chaste self is becoming central. Cohesion is good - chastity aligns with values and relationship. Some diffusion from frustration but overall coherent."@en .

:id_anne_split a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Split Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Split/dual" ; :identityCohesion "0.5" ; :identityDiffusion "0.5" ; :description "Identity is split between mistress and penitent. Two selves coexist uneasily. Mistress is public, penitent is private. Integration is growth task - finding way to honor both. Split creates internal tension but also flexibility."@en .

:id_becky_transitioning a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Transitioning Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "In transition" ; :identityCohesion "0.5" ; :identityDiffusion "0.5" ; :description "Identity is in active transition from college student to slave. Two identities coexist uneasily. Student identity is fading, slave identity is strengthening. Integration will involve finding way to honor both or choosing slave as primary. This is core developmental task."@en .

:id_beth_servant a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Servant Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Servant/employee" ; :identityCohesion "0.8" ; :identityDiffusion "0.2" ; :description "Identity is organized around service role. Cohesion is high - role is clear. Some diffusion from class shame but overall coherent. Identity is stable but limiting."@en .

:id_bree_fragmented a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Fragmented Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Fragmented/compartmentalized" ; :identityCohesion "0.5" ; :identityDiffusion "0.6" ; :description "Identity is split between professional self (curious, brave, truth-seeking) and personal self (traditional, anxious, shame-based). These selves don't communicate well. Professional self can explore topics personal self finds threatening. Integration of these selves is key growth task."@en .

:id_edward_fragile a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Fragile Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Fragile/conflicted" ; :identityCohesion "0.4" ; :identityDiffusion "0.6" ; :description "Identity is fragile and conflicted. Servant vs. deserving, anger vs. fear. Cohesion is low, diffusion is high. This creates instability and unpredictability."@en .

:id_leo_integrated a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Integrated Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Integrated" ; :identityCohesion "0.9" ; :identityDiffusion "0.1" ; :description "Identity is highly integrated. Dominant self, professional self, personal self all coherent. No significant internal conflict. This integration is strength but also rigidity. Growth would involve allowing more complexity."@en .

:id_max_keyholder a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Keyholder Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Keyholder/dominant" ; :identityCohesion "0.85" ; :identityDiffusion "0.15" ; :description "Identity is organized around keyholder role. Cohesion is high - keyholder aligns with values and desires. Some diffusion from conventional expectations but overall coherent."@en .

:id_nolan_integrated a :IdentityStructure ; rdfs:label "Integrated Identity Structure"@en ; :identityType "Integrated/cohesive" ; :identityCohesion "0.9" ; :identityDiffusion "0.1" ; :description "Highly integrated identity. Professional, sexual, personal selves are aligned. No compartmentalization needed. This integration is result of long inner work. Makes him effective leader but also creates impatience with those still struggling (like Bree). Growth involves remembering his own journey."@en .

:io_alice_romantic a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Romantic Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Romantic/emotional" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.8" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.85" ; :description "Romantic intimacy orientation. Intimacy through emotional connection, not just sex. Capacity for non-sexual intimacy is high. Willingness is high. Intimacy supports chastity."@en .

:io_anne_protected a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Protected Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Protected/guarded" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.5" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.4" ; :description "Intimacy is protected and guarded. Capable of intimacy but guarded. BDSM intimacy feels safer than emotional intimacy. Willingness is low - intimacy requires vulnerability she avoids."@en .

:io_becky_opening a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Opening Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Opening" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.7" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.8" ; :description "Intimacy orientation is opening through training. Vulnerability during scenes builds intimacy capacity. Willingness is high - wants closeness with Leo/Anne. Intimacy is through service and surrender."@en .

:io_beth_closed a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Closed Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Closed/protected" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.3" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.2" ; :description "Intimacy is closed and protected. Employment boundary limits intimacy. Capacity is low, willingness is low. Intimacy would complicate employment."@en .

:io_bree_avoidant a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Avoidant Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Avoidant/protected" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.5" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.3" ; :description "Avoids deep intimacy, especially sexual/emotional. Single at 29 partly due to intimacy avoidance. Professional relationships feel safer than personal ones. Intimacy capacity exists but willingness is low. BDSM exploration may require developing intimacy tolerance."@en .

:io_edward_closed a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Closed Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Closed/hostile" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.2" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.2" ; :description "Intimacy is closed and hostile. Incapable of healthy intimacy. Capacity is minimal, willingness is minimal. Intimacy would require major work."@en .

:io_leo_selective a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Selective Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Selective/limited" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.5" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.4" ; :description "Intimacy is selective and limited. Capable of intimacy but chooses carefully. BDSM intimacy (power exchange) feels safer than emotional intimacy. Willingness is low - intimacy requires vulnerability."@en .

:io_max_emotional a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Emotional Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Emotional/commitment" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.75" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.7" ; :description "Emotional intimacy orientation. Intimacy through commitment, not just sex. Capacity is good, willingness is good. Chastity enhances emotional intimacy for him."@en .

:io_nolan_selective a :IntimacyOrientation ; rdfs:label "Selective Intimacy Orientation"@en ; :intimacyType "Selective/protected" ; :intimacyCapacity "0.7" ; :intimacyWillingness "0.5" ; :description "Capable of intimacy but selective about partners. Professional distance protects against over-involvement. Intimacy requires trust and time. With Bree, intimacy may develop through education process - sharing knowledge is form of intimacy."@en .

:ip_exclusive_interview a :InterviewProtocol ; rdfs:label "Exclusive BDSM Club Interview Protocol"@en ; :interviewProtocolType "Investigative journalism, exclusive access" ; :interviewProtocolDuration "Multiple sessions, 2 weeks" ; :description "Protocol for interviewing BDSM club owner and members. Includes: initial phone contact, in-person interview, club tour, member interviews, consent documentation, fact-checking."@en ; :usedBy :c_bree ; :usedOn :c_nolan .

:ja_black_collar a :JournalisticAssignment ; rdfs:label "The Black Collar Investigation"@en ; :journalisticAssignmentType "Investigative journalism, BDSM club exposé" ; :journalisticAssignmentDeadline "2 weeks" ; :description "Bree Barrett assigned by Chase Murdock to investigate The Black Collar exclusive BDSM club. Exclusive access granted by owner Nolan Carter. Story driven by public interest and rumors of brothel activities."@en ; :assignedBy :c_chase ; :assignedTo :c_bree ; :about :venue_black_collar .

:mf_alice_conventional a :MoralFramework ; rdfs:label "Conventional Moral Framework"@en ; :moralType "Conventional" ; :moralRigidity "0.6" ; :moralFlexibility "0.5" ; :description "Moral framework is conventional with BDSM adaptation. Traditional values (marriage, commitment) are core. Chastity is unconventional but framed as traditional (purity). Flexibility is moderate."@en .

:mf_anne_evolving a :MoralFramework ; rdfs:label "Evolving Moral Framework"@en ; :moralType "Transitional" ; :moralRigidity "0.4" ; :moralFlexibility "0.6" ; :description "Moral framework in evolution. Betrayal shattered old framework. New framework is emerging: redemption through service, honesty, BDSM ethics. Flexibility is high because in transition. Eventually will solidify."@en .

:mf_becky_evolving a :MoralFramework ; rdfs:label "Evolving Moral Framework"@en ; :moralType "Transitional" ; :moralRigidity "0.4" ; :moralFlexibility "0.7" ; :description "Moral framework in evolution from conventional (college, independence) to BDSM-aligned (service, ownership). Flexibility is high because she's in transition. Eventually will solidify around service and ownership ethics."@en .

:mf_beth_duty a :MoralFramework ; rdfs:label "Duty-Based Moral Framework"@en ; :moralType "Duty-based" ; :moralRigidity "0.7" ; :moralFlexibility "0.3" ; :description "Moral framework is duty-based. Duty determines right action. Framework is rigid - duty above all. This enables endurance but limits ethical reflection."@en .

:mf_bree_religious a :MoralFramework ; rdfs:label "Religious Moral Framework"@en ; :moralType "Religious/deontological" ; :moralRigidity "0.75" ; :moralFlexibility "0.3" ; :description "Moral framework based on religious teachings. Sex outside marriage = wrong. Submission = virtuous. Curiosity about taboo = dangerous. Framework is rigid with low flexibility. Encountering BDSM consent ethics (SSC, RACK) will challenge this framework. May need to develop more flexible, consent-based morality."@en .

