:rn_beth_clear_expectations a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Clear Expectations"@en ; :needType "Clarity/structure" ; :needIntensity "0.8" ; :needFulfillment "0.8" ; :description "High need for clear expectations. Anne's rules provide this. Clarity reduces anxiety. Need is well-fulfilled."@en .

:rn_beth_security a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Job Security"@en ; :needType "Security/stability" ; :needIntensity "0.95" ; :needFulfillment "0.7" ; :description "Overwhelming need for job security. Employment is survival. This drives all behavior. Need is partially fulfilled but anxiety remains."@en .

:rn_bree_safety a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Safety"@en ; :needType "Physical/emotional safety" ; :needIntensity "0.9" ; :needFulfillment "0.6" ; :description "High need for safety and predictability. Control provides sense of safety. BDSM exploration threatens this need. Requires clear boundaries, consent, and predictability to feel safe enough to explore. Nolan's professionalism and explicit consent practices can provide this."@en .

:rn_bree_validation a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Validation"@en ; :needType "Approval/validation" ; :needIntensity "0.8" ; :needFulfillment "0.5" ; :description "High need for external validation and approval. From parents (conditional), friends (traditional expectations), now Chase (professional approval). May seek Nolan's validation that she's 'good' even while exploring 'bad' topics. Growth involves developing internal validation."@en .

:rn_edward_belonging a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Belonging"@en ; :needType "Belonging/acceptance" ; :needIntensity "0.8" ; :needFulfillment "0.2" ; :description "High need for belonging. Isolated, doesn't belong. Fulfillment is minimal. Loneliness fuels resentment and volatility."@en .

:rn_edward_respect a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Respect"@en ; :needType "Respect/recognition" ; :needIntensity "0.9" ; :needFulfillment "0.1" ; :description "Overwhelming need for respect. Feels constantly disrespected. Fulfillment is minimal - perceives contempt everywhere. This drives resentment."@en .

:rn_leo_compliance a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Compliance"@en ; :needType "Compliance/control" ; :needIntensity "0.9" ; :needFulfillment "0.85" ; :description "High need for compliance. Partners must follow rules, protocols, directions. Compliance is proof of submission. Becky's improving compliance satisfies this need. Non-compliance triggers punishment."@en .

:rn_leo_respect a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Respect/Obedience"@en ; :needType "Respect/obedience" ; :needIntensity "0.95" ; :needFulfillment "0.8" ; :description "Absolute need for respect and obedience. Disrespect is intolerable. Obedience is baseline expectation. Training ensures obedience. Need is non-negotiable - relationships without it are impossible."@en .

:rn_max_control a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Control"@en ; :needType "Control/ownership" ; :needIntensity "0.85" ; :needFulfillment "0.9" ; :description "High need for control of Alice's sexuality. This is core need, not preference. Fulfillment is high - Alice is locked and compliant. Need is non-negotiable."@en .

:rn_max_loyalty a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Loyalty"@en ; :needType "Loyalty/fidelity" ; :needIntensity "0.9" ; :needFulfillment "0.95" ; :description "Very high need for loyalty. Chastity ensures fidelity. Loyalty is proof of commitment. Need is well-fulfilled. Disloyalty would be devastating."@en .

:rn_nolan_respect a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Respect"@en ; :needType "Respect/recognition" ; :needIntensity "0.8" ; :needFulfillment "0.8" ; :description "Need for respect as community leader and individual. Respect is earned through competence and ethics. Doesn't need approval but needs respect. Bree shows respect through professional approach, which he values."@en .

:rn_nolan_understanding a :RelationalNeed ; rdfs:label "Need for Understanding"@en ; :needType "Being understood" ; :needIntensity "0.7" ; :needFulfillment "0.5" ; :description "Need to be understood by outsiders. Tired of being misunderstood as abuser or deviant. Bree represents opportunity for understanding through journalism. This need motivates cooperation despite risks."@en .

