:sc_alice_chaste a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "Chaste Woman Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am a chaste woman, locked for Max, sexually denied" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.75" ; :selfConceptStability "0.7" ; :description "Chaste identity is developing. Locked, denied, sexually frustrated but committed. This identity is newer and less stable than fiancee identity. Integration of fiancee and chaste selves is ongoing."@en .

:sc_alice_fiancee a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "Fiancee Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am Max's fiancee, preparing for marriage and life together" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.85" ; :selfConceptStability "0.8" ; :description "Fiancee identity is central. Preparing for marriage, building life with Max. This identity is stable and clear. Chastity is part of fiancee role. Identity is conventional (fiancee) with unconventional element (chastity)."@en .

:sc_anne_mistress a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "Mistress Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am mistress of household, dominant over Becky and Beth" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.8" ; :selfConceptStability "0.7" ; :description "Mistress identity is clear but not absolute. Dominant over Becky (training) and Beth (servant). This identity is source of power and redemption. Through dominance, she serves Leo. Identity is stable but complicated by penitent self."@en .

:sc_anne_penitent a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "Penitent Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am penitent, seeking redemption for betraying Leo" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.7" ; :selfConceptStability "0.6" ; :description "Penitent identity coexists with mistress identity. Guilt drives need for redemption. Submission to Leo is penance. This identity is less stable - questions about whether redemption is possible. Penitent self is private, mistress self is public."@en .

:sc_becky_slave a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "Slave Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am Leo and Anne's slave in training, learning to serve and belong" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.7" ; :selfConceptStability "0.6" ; :description "Slave identity is strengthening through training. Feels more authentic than student identity. Negotiated shared ownership (7 weeks Anne, 2 weekends Leo) shows investment in slave identity. This identity will likely become primary as training completes."@en .

:sc_becky_student a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "College Student Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am a college sophomore, undeclared major, figuring out my future" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.5" ; :selfConceptStability "0.4" ; :description "College student identity is becoming less clear. Undeclared major reflects broader uncertainty. Slave identity feels more real than student identity. May eventually leave college or find way to integrate both selves. Currently in transition."@en .

:sc_beth_invisible a :SelfConcept ; rdfs:label "Invisible Person Identity"@en ; :selfConceptContent "I am invisible, unnoticed, background" ; :selfConceptClarity "0.7" ; :selfConceptStability "0.7" ; :description "Identity as invisible person. Not seen as individual but as function. This is both protection and wound. Invisibility enables service but denies personhood."@en .

