# The Inheritance - Themes

:theme_femdom_inheritance a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Female Domination"@en ;
    :description "Female domination (femdom) is the central theme. Mary takes control as Mistress, commanding Joe's submission, labor, and sexual denial. The power exchange is explicit and negotiated, with Mary as the dominant figure who uses Joe for service and pleasure."@en .

:theme_maleSubmission a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Male Submission and Masochism"@en ;
    :description "Joe represents the male masochist who finds deep satisfaction in submission. His desire to serve, be humiliated, and denied is portrayed as a genuine need rather than performance. He craves female control as a fundamental part of his identity."@en .

:theme_feminization a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Feminization and Sissification"@en ;
    :description "Joe is feminized through wearing women's underwear, shaving his body hair, eventually wearing maid outfits with breasts and makeup. This represents the ultimate submission - giving up masculinity."@en .

:theme_chastity a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Chastity and Denial"@en ;
    :description "Chastity play is prominent - Joe wears a metal tube device that prevents erection and orgasm. His sexual pleasure comes only through serving Mary's needs. Denial becomes a form of worship."@en .

:theme_cuckolding a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Cuckolding"@en ;
    :description "Mary cuckolds Joe by bringing other men (Allen) to their bedroom while Joe is locked in his cage or present. Joe's arousal at this humiliation is a key element of his masochism."@en .

:theme_serviceSubmission a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Service Submission"@en ;
    :description "Submission is expressed through service - Joe does all the restoration work on the mansion, cooking, cleaning, farm labor. His value comes from his labor and obedience rather than sexual performance."@en .

:theme_restorationRedemption a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Restoration as Redemption"@en ;
    :description "Restoring the old mansion serves as a metaphor for restoring relationships and self. Mary rebuilds both the house and her life through Joe's help. The plantation represents legacy and renewal."@en .

:theme_religionVsDesire a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Religion Versus Desire"@en ;
    :description "The conflict between religious morality (Tiffany, the church) and sexual desire is explored. Tiffany initially judges Mary's lifestyle but eventually embraces it herself. The church represents external judgment that cannot compete with internal truth."@en .


