## Themes - They Also Serve

:theme_slavery a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Slavery and Indenture"@en ;
    :description "The story explores institutional slavery through indentured contracts, the Slave Warehouse cage system, control collars, and slave training boutiques. Terry signs away his freedom to avoid labor battalion."@en .

:theme_genderTransformation a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Gender Transformation"@en ;
    :description "Terry undergoes genetic sex change from male to female due to limited job prospects as an unintelligent male. The story follows his transition and adaptation to female identity."@en .

:theme_powerExchange a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Power Exchange and Control"@en ;
    :description "Control collars, brain scanners, and command streams create explicit power dynamics. Slave Devotion psychologically binds slaves to their contracts."@en .

:theme_identity a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Identity and Self"@en ;
    :description "Terry struggles with becoming Terri. The story explores how identity shifts with body modification and social role changes from male worker to female slave."@en .

:theme_service a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Service and Submission"@en ;
    :description "Various forms of service - household robots, maids, Statues who hold poses for hours. Service is the primary value assigned to slaves."@en .

:theme_submission a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Submission and Obedience"@en ;
    :description "Basic Collar Obedience training, robot command streams, and slave devotion poetry establish patterns of submission."@en .

:theme_acceptance a :Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Acceptance and Adaptation"@en ;
    :description "Terry/Terri adapts to each stage of transformation and training, eventually finding satisfaction as a Statue - 'a job she could handle.'"@en .

